# This file IS an OpenSSH allowed_signers file. It is meant to be used verbatim:
#
#     curl -sO https://colophonmethod.com/.well-known/colophon/keys
#     ssh-keygen -Y verify -f keys -I f.chinaglia@gmail.com -n colophon \
#                -Overify-time=YYYYMMDD -s events.jsonl.sig < events.jsonl
#
# It is an append-only history, not a current-key file. A retired line keeps its
# valid-before and stays; nothing is ever deleted. Because a register is timestamped,
# rotating a key invalidates nothing: a reader asks whether the key was valid at the
# moment the timestamp says the signature existed, which is what -Overify-time does.
#
# What this proves, and what it does not. It proves that whoever controlled
# colophonmethod.com and its TLS certificate published this key. It does not prove
# who that is, and no file can: a key is bound to a person by evidence outside the
# artefact it signs, which is exactly why this file is not inside the repository whose
# cases it authenticates.

